{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"The cached system library is Jansson 2.14, while the reference is 2.15 and adds allocator-v2 behavior plus private exports. Using it as the implementation would create subtle allocator and bug-fix mismatches, so I’m not treating it as the translation. I’m now inspecting the exact data layouts and implementation boundaries to port the core object model first, followed by parser/dumper and the variadic ABI entry points."}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"I have enough layout information to begin the implementation. I’m creating a dependency-light Rust crate with explicit C layouts, stable allocation addresses for object iterators, C-compatible reference counting, and separate modules for values, loading, dumping, pack/unpack, and the leaked private ABI; the variadic entry points will use small System V ABI shims that hand a real `va_list` to Rust."}}
